 [asy]
pair A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H, M, N, P;
A = (0, 2);
B = rotate(45)*A;
C = rotate(45)*B;
D = rotate(45)*C;
E = 1.2*abs(C + A + B)/2;
F = 1.2*abs(A + C + D)/2;
G = 1.2*abs(C + D + E)/2;
H = 1.2*abs(D + E + F)/2;
M = (G + F)/2;
N = (B + D)/2;
P = 0.4*abs(C + D + E + F)/4 + 0.6*abs(G + H)/4;
draw(A--B--C--D--E--F--G--H--cycle);
draw(A--P--H);

label("$A$", A, SW);
label("$B$", B, NW);
label("$C$", C, N);
label("$D$", D, NE);
label("$E$", E, N);
label("$F$", F, NNE);
label("$G$", G, ENE);
label("$H$", H, E);
label("$P$", P, NE);

[/asy]

Think: Notice that vertices of the octagon divide the square into 16 equal isosceles triangles. From now on, we will use the notation $O$ to designate any of the 16 vertex points.

Now, draw lines $D$ to $M$, $F$ to $N$ that divide the octagon into 8 isosceles triangles. This creates 4 smaller isosceles triangles that are half the size of each isosceles triangles formed by $O_D, O_F, O_G$ and $O_H.$

[asy]
pair A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H, M, N, P, O_D, O_F, O_G, O_H;
A = (0, 2);
